+    # (intentionally: one cookie per browser, one decoder per layer). They
+    # differ by the ``type`` claim — ``"portal"`` for portal sessions, absent
+    # for agency sessions. Decoding a portal token here would surface its
+    # ``sub`` (a ``client_id``) as a ``user_id``, and although ``db.get(User,
+    # client_uuid)`` happens to miss (a client id is not a user id) and the
+    # caller lands on 401, the safe behaviour is to reject the token at the
+    # type layer instead of relying on a database lookup to fail. This is
+    # the same check ``decode_portal_token`` already applies in reverse.
     try:
         payload = jwt.decode(token, get_settings().secret_key, algorithms=["HS256"])
